+# HIL Runbook — production checklist (vendor agnostic)
+
+Scope
+- Use this runbook to execute HIL runs safely, collect evidence and escalate if needed.
+
+Preconditions
+- All engineers on the run must be trained and acknowledged.
+- E-STOP hardware endpoint tested and reachable.
+- Network isolation in place (VLAN) for HIL.
+- Evidence bucket credentials available and tested.
+
+Basic flow
+1. Verify E-STOP stub / hardware using ops/robotics/estop/estop_stub.py or vendor API.
+2. Run sensor-only Stage A (ops/robotics/hil/vendor_X/hil_test_case.py).
+3. Validate telemetry and cosign the evidence bundle (ops/production/generate_signoff_package.py).
+4. Proceed to Stage B (limited actuation) under direct operator control.
+5. Monitor E-STOP latency and telemetry channels; if any anomaly, trigger E-STOP and abort.
+6. Upload signed evidence and mark HIL scenario complete.
+
+Escalation
+- If any safety condition fails, immediately engage E-STOP and notify Safety Owner and Platform Ops.
+
